Run 1: `add acme/json@2.2.0 --file ws/apps/b/main.roc`. Member b has no json, and a holds 2.0.0, so the new entry has the range `=2.2.0` and the json of a is movable (R-WS12, R-SP23). The first search has no tuple. The second search moves json to 2.2.0 (the nearest value that works: 2.0.5 and 2.1.0 fail). The index of the movable groups (pfx, yaml) is read after the first search (R-DI1): the log has no index call for them before that. The ladder runs on the new tuple (6 probes: a and b), then the report on stderr, then exit 13: no answer, no write (R-SP16, R-SP17, R-EC13). The version that the user named is not hidden by `min-release-age` for the new entry and for the json of a (R-C7: the note is printed once).
Run 2: the same with `--json`: the mode is non-interactive for `--json` (R-NM3), stdout is the envelope with `error.details.moves[]` (alias, name, from, to, why, members: the files that the move writes, R-SP25, R-J5).
Run 3: the same with `--dry-run`: the report, the header diff with the moves (a: `~ json`, b: `+ json`, the `talon.toml` key), no prompt, exit 0, nothing written (R-SP26, R-LF4).
