Run 5: run 1 with `--allow-moves`: the flag answers R-NI3 (R-SP17, R-NM10). The move is written to a (`~ json`) and b gets the new entry (`+ json`), the key `json = "=2.2.0"` is the key of the new entry (R-AD22, R-AD23).
Run 6: `update yaml@1.1.0 --yes`: yaml is free (R-SP5), `yaml 1.1.0` names pf 0.1.1 and the platform is held at 0.1.0 by both members. No tuple in the first search. The second search moves the platform to 0.1.1, and the move writes both members that have the entry (R-SP25, R-WS11). `--yes` answers R-NI3 (R-NM10). json (anchored by run 5) and lex stay.
